Part of this rise is simply that there are far more e-bikes on the road than there were 20 years ago. These records do not include sales, so they cannot say whether e-bikes are recalled more often per bike sold than conventional bikes.

What fails on e-bikes
E-bikes inherit every failure a conventional bike can have, and add one of their own. The electrical system (battery, charger, motor, controller, and wiring) accounts for 37% of e-bike recall events. The rest are the familiar parts: forks, frames, brakes, wheels, and handlebars, now carrying more weight at higher speeds.

